## 3. What the counter means

# The skip happens in drawIndexedInstancedDetour: the exact call is the first
# DrawIndexedInstanced(6,1) of the list whose bind-time tag equals this frame's arg10
# (EXP-0066), and the detour returns without forwarding -> the draw is not recorded into
# the command list and never reaches ExecuteCommandLists. #1200 over ~13 s at ~60 fps
# is one skip per frame; `skipped=1` on the injection side is the single arm-frame skip,
# so the DLSS write replaced every one of those frames.
# Caveat: the frame-shape line still counts this list as "d1" because the detour keeps
# sig->draws in sync with a normal frame; the skip counter above, not the shape line,
# is the evidence for F1.
